# What cad does as an interpreter starts, on Python 3.15 and later (PEP 829), which then ignores cad.pth's import
# lines; earlier Pythons run cad.pth's and never read this file. The same two steps, in the same order: the release
# that runs (_cad_release), then `import build123d` made lazy (lazy_kernel).
_cad_release:start
cad._internal.lazy_kernel:install
